    "path": "/policies/vaccinations",
    "type": "landing",
    "title": "Vaccination Requirements | UnSaid Memories Memphis",
    "metaDescription": "Current rabies vaccination proof required for all grooming appointments. Vaccine must be given at least 24 hours before the visit.",
    "h1": "Vaccination Requirements",
    "copyParagraphs": [
      "Every pet groomed at UnSaid Memories must have current rabies vaccination proof on file, and the vaccine must have been administered at least 24 hours before the appointment. No exceptions — this protects your pet, the other pets in the salon, and our staff.",
      "A grooming salon is a shared space: multiple animals, close contact, hours together. Rabies is a serious, preventable disease, and the 24-hour window ensures the vaccine has had time to take effect. This is standard practice at professional grooming salons nationwide, and it's one of the simplest ways we keep the salon safe for everyone.",
      "- A current rabies certificate from your veterinarian (paper or digital photo is fine) - Veterinary records showing the vaccination date and expiration - Upload it to your account before the appointment, or bring it to check-in",
      "If your pet was vaccinated yesterday, you're good. If they were vaccinated this morning, the appointment needs to move — the 24-hour rule is firm. When in doubt, reschedule rather than risk a turned-away appointment.",
      "If your records are expired or you can't locate them, book with your vet first, then book with us once the 24-hour window has passed. We cannot groom a pet without valid proof, and we can't waive the requirement at check-in.",
      "Young pets follow the same rule: current rabies vaccination, given at least 24 hours before the visit, with proof on file. Talk to your vet about timing their first groom around their vaccination schedule.",
      "Not sure if your documentation qualifies? Message us through the contact form or bring it to a free consultation and we'll confirm before you book."
    ],
