    "path": "/process",
    "type": "landing",
    "title": "Our Grooming Process — What to Expect | UnSaid Memories",
    "metaDescription": "From check-in to pickup: what happens during your pet's grooming appointment at our Memphis salon, including pre-check-in.",
    "h1": "How Grooming Works at UnSaid Memories",
    "copyParagraphs": [
      "Book online in a few minutes: choose your service, pick a time, and complete pre-check-in from your account. Pre-check-in is where you tell us the important stuff — sensitivities, past grooming experiences, the cut you want, your vet's contact. Your answers write back to your pet's customer record, so every future visit starts with us already knowing them. Bring current rabies vaccination proof (the vaccine must have been given at least 24 hours before the appointment).",
      "When you arrive, a groomer does a hands-on assessment: coat type and condition, skin check, nail length, ear condition, temperament read. We confirm the service, the cut, and the exact price with you. If we find matting or a skin concern that changes the plan, we discuss it now — before anything starts, and with your approval.",
      "Warm water, shampoo matched to your pet's coat and skin (oatmeal for sensitive, clarifying for oily, deshedding formulas when booked), a thorough double rinse, and careful fluff drying. Cats and anxious dogs get the calmest version of this: lower dryer settings, breaks as needed, and a groomer who watches body language the whole time.",
      "For bath-and-haircut appointments, the groomer works to the cut you approved at check-in — breed standard, pet trim, puppy cut, teddy bear, summer short. We work in sections, checking symmetry and blending as we go, and we never rush the face: it's the part you see first at pickup.",
      "Every groom includes a nail trim (grinding available as an add-on), ear cleaning, and finishing touches — a brush-out, a spritz, a bandana or bow if you like. Then a final once-over: we check our own work the way you'd check it at home.",
      "You get a text when your pet is ready. At pickup, your groomer gives you a quick report: how they did, anything we noticed (a hot spot, a tender nail, a skin change worth mentioning to your vet), and when we'd recommend the next visit. The full notes go into your pet's record for next time.",
      "Your pet's record keeps everything: services, treatments, notes, preferences. Next booking takes seconds because pre-check-in is already half done. Bath Club members are on recurring schedules and skip the remembering entirely."
    ],
