      "The main pharmacy shelf for feline parasite prevention: topical treatments, oral medications, and collars that kill and repel fleas and ticks. Memphis's long warm season makes fleas a nearly year-round concern here — indoor cats included, since fleas hitchhike in on people and other pets. The non-negotiable rule of this category: use cat-specific products only. Dog flea treatments containing permethrin are fatally toxic to cats, so never substitute and never split a dog dose. Match the product to your cat's weight and lifestyle, apply topicals exactly as directed, and treat all pets in the household simultaneously or the fleas just relocate. For the delivery method that suits your cat, compare Flea Drops for Cats, Cat Flea & Tick Pills & Chews, and Cat Flea & Tick Collars; our MidSouth flea-and-tick guide covers the seasonal plan for the Flea & Tick Solutions for Cats department. Treat every pet in the home on the same day and mark it on the calendar; staggered schedules leave untreated hosts for fleas to retreat to, and the infestation simply migrates."
